o like a big name company or  something like that  or anything on steam or you know  anything like that just a lot of little  demos and a lot of little samples  and  i think it's time for me to change that  and  yeah so i'm going to start working on  the the game extended stay that i  somewhat talked about in a previous  video  and i don't know exactly how it's going  to go but i intend to start putting out  stuff for it and start working towards  it in this next year  and this whole engine here my old  ancient archer engine which has moved  into the private space  that's what this is going to be built to  support so i'm going to build it on my  own engine and this engine is going to  be built to support the game i'm making  and i don't know where it's going to go  one of the reasons i decided to make  this the future iterations of this  engine private is because well  it's complicated but basically i don't  know where i'm going to take it  exactly and  until then i don't really feel like it's  a good idea to just kind of like  pull in different directions all the  time and not really know i don't know  how to explain it other than that and  also i guess you know one of the bigger  things is i'm gonna have  other libraries attached to it that are  to do with this game i'm gonna make and  obviously i don't want to release all  that source code and stuff before i even  release the game so i'm trying to keep  i'm trying to figure out what to keep  private and whatnot but it's a it's a  complicated thing now what i thought  about doing is just making like a public  version of this specifically for the  channel and when i work on it i can  maybe stream it on  youtube or something and we can also  take contributions from other people  that watch the channel and want to add  in their stuff because making a game  engine  once you've  kind of dove into the main stuff you can  recreate it up to where you are pretty  quickly it's making those  incremental advancements to next 