ady did  one of cameras that's kind of maybe a  sample  really long that one but i want to do  that for like a lot of different aspects  of game engine as i go because those are  videos i can throw together quickly and  not try to  distract too much a lot of the problems  i had in the past  was that i would make these giant  productions  of little things  like how to use c plus plus and visuals  studio or something like that like if  you know the knowledge you can just kind  of put it out there  but for me i felt like i had to make it  a big production and  that would make it a lot more watchable  and i think in part that's what helped  me grow but also that started to lead to  burnout  and i don't think it would have led to  burnout if i like secured finances to  get an editor but i that didn't happen  so i was doing the editing  you know just the whole nine yards it  was just too much and basically what  ended up happening last year that i  think really drove me to the point of  almost quitting  was that i found that i was spending a  lot more time stressing and worrying  about making these videos than actually  living my dream of just like  being a really good programmer and  putting out  actual software like i basically all the  the software basically took a backseat  and it was all about this  social thing of you youtube which  you might have figured out  by now that i don't really i don't  really get off on the whole social media  thing i don't particularly care how many  people follow me or don't follow me or  and stuff like that i'm i'm just not  that type of person it's and it's not to  say that i don't like it i mean it's  tricky for me to even get right in my  own head like  there's a there's a big part of me  that doesn't particularly care what  other people do i'm always just kind of  focused on my own thing  and that's it has its advantages but  that also has some downsides too  and i guess i could talk about that  briefly like the biggest downside of 